A||||25||REDHOTT88||2.8 V6 Horsepower: Is that at the rear wheels?||||5||
Z||000000||REDHOTT88||12-03-2001||03:49 PM||||I had a friend ask about the Fieros' horsepower. I had always heard the 2.8L V6 had around 130-140 HP, so I told him that.<P>Then he asked if it was at the flywheel or the rear wheels. I honestly never thought about that.... Can anyone help me out with some HP knowledge? <P>I imagine since there is no driveshaft, it wouldn't be that much of a difference... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed<BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red & shiny all over!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||12-03-2001||03:54 PM||||Manufacture advertised engine horse power is at fly wheel.  I think the number drops about 18% through drivetrain to wheels?||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||12-03-2001||04:27 PM||||the following graphs are HP/TQ at the wheels...<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiraldyno.jpg">   <P>bone stock V6 no mods, stock timing, fuel, intake, exhaust.<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstdyno_manymods.jpg">   <BR>after tuning, exh, intake, fuel, timing fuel pressure and injector duty cycle manipulated (S-afc) and TV cable clamped.<P>yep at the rated hp/tq is at the flywheel. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst2m6sig_1.gif">   <P> <A HREF="http://www.1fst2m6.com" TARGET=_blank>www.1fst2m6.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||12-03-2001||04:38 PM||||Thanks...   I'm no Technician by any means, so looking at the graphs, I'm like DUH!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>What would be an average HP at the wheels?<P>Assuming your car is tuned, kept up, and runs decent?<BR>||||reg||1
