Z||000005||REDHOTT88||12-03-2001||06:51 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by lou_dias:<BR><B>damn my old dyno sheet is looking good.<BR>I know I keep saying it but my next 3.4 will be done soon.  Can't wait to dyno that one.  too bad it's not a total rebuild, the block has 60k on it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeaahhh.... THAT was helpful...thanks I guess. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>||||reg||11
Z||000006||avengador1||12-03-2001||07:05 PM||||The horsepower rating is at the flywheel without driveline loses but with accesories hooked up(alternator, ac compressor, etc.). In the sixties cars were rated at gross horsepower, that rating was without any accesories attached to the engine and no driveline loses, so the numbers were always big. So the horsepower numbers for the Fiero are not at the rear wheels as shown by the charts posted. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||lou_dias||12-03-2001||07:15 PM||||1fstm6 has my old dyno sheet.<BR>It's a rebuilt 3.4 w/poorly portes and NOT polished heads, slightly ported lower and middle intake, Sprint F1 headers, Crane 2030 Compucam, Mangnum 1.52 roller rockers, hollow cat, IRM mufferless dual exhaust, K&N, SpiralMax (lost 3.4 hp there), no air silencer (so I didn't have cool air either).<BR>I made just about 147hp and 203ft*lbs of torque.<P>Next one is a 3.4 w/60k miles, real ported and polished heads, ported TB and upper intake, the previously mention middle and lower intake, 1.52 rockers, stock camaro cam and the previously mentioned exhaust setup an K&N, NO spiralmax this time and I need to get me a WCF Velocity tube.<P>I'm hoping for 160+hp 200 torque.||||reg||1
Z||000008||LoW_KeY||12-03-2001||09:16 PM||||Hmm I know my 2.8 was probably putting out about 170, my friends was putting 198 at the wheels and that was a stock 2.8! <P>I think there are some odd 2.8's out there in some of our fieros my 3.4 only feels a tad bit faster in the higher rpm ranges, think after the rebuild it'll be a whole new story  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>-KC<P><P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000009||Nashco||12-03-2001||10:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LoW_KeY:<BR><B>Hmm I know my 2.8 was probably putting out about 170, my friends was putting 198 at the wheels and that was a stock 2.8! <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Stock what...stock valve covers?  198 at the wheels with a <B>completely</B> stock 2.8....wow, I'll definitely be the first to say, "I'll believe it when I see it."<P>Sorry to be a skeptic...but no way, in my eyes.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||Standard||12-03-2001||10:01 PM||||198 at the wheels with a stock 2.8?  sorry,  but I'm gonna have to call  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  Unless you have the dyno sheets to prove it... That would be 230-240 HP at the flywheel, and that kind of power is just not possible w/o a built-to-the-hilt 2.8, and it would also probably have to be carb'd, unless you go to an aftermarket engine controller and/or have access to a lot of time on the dyno and a prom burner.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000011||1FST2M6||12-04-2001||08:25 AM||||Lous dyno sheet...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  3.4..<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/loudyno.jpg">  <P><BR>NO WAY 198hp... HA.. dyno sheet or not... you'd need like 14:1 compression a HELLUVA lot of head work and a TECII to control it. it's taken me 3 years to break 200hp and i'm spraying!  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
